pragma cashscript ^0.14.0;

// Grandma's Wallet shared authorization interface, v2.
//
// A protected output (wallet funds or an application position) is bound to a
// wallet identity: the token category of the wallet's controller. It may only
// be spent in a transaction that the current owner of that identity approves.
//
// Transaction layout:
//   Inputs:  00-controller, 01+ protected inputs and anything else
//   Outputs: 00-controller, 01+ anything
//
// A protected output holds no key and checks no signature. It requires that
//   - input 0 is the wallet's controller, and
//   - the controller continues with the same owner, epoch, recoverer and
//     delay, and with no recovery claim pending.
//
// The controller is spent in the same transaction and enforces its own rules.
// Only its owner-signed functions can produce that successor: a recovery
// request leaves a claim pending and a completed recovery changes the owner
// and epoch. The owner's signature, which the controller requires to cover
// every input and output, is therefore what approves the protected spend.
//
// The presence of the controller alone is not treated as approval: the
// recoverer can also spend it, to request or complete recovery, and neither
// satisfies the second requirement.
//
// A controller that offered any way to reach that successor without the
// owner's signature would break this interface. The version byte of the
// state identifies the controller rules this version was written against.
function ownerApproves(bytes32 identity) {
    // The genuine controller: the identity NFT with mutable capability.
    require(tx.inputs[0].tokenCategory == identity + 0x01);

    bytes state = tx.inputs[0].nftCommitment;
    require(state.length == 69);
    require(state.split(1)[0] == 0x01);

    require(tx.outputs[0].tokenCategory == identity + 0x01);
    require(
        tx.outputs[0].nftCommitment ==
            0x0100 + state.slice(2, 49) + 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    );
}
